#   Comments + Keyword Clarification

#    Anton, Calculus, 2.6.50
# DESCRIPTION
# Find the derivative of a function using the chain rule

# ENDDESCRIPTION
## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Differentiation)
## DBsection(Chain rule (without trigonometric functions))
## Institution(John Wiley & Sons)
## Level(2)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Anton')
## EditionText1('9')
## Section1('2.6')
## Problem1('50')
## KEYWORDS('Derivative', 'Chain rule', 'tangent line')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'contextFraction.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Numeric")->variables->add(u => 'Real');

$a   = random(2, 8);
$b   = random(1, 4, 3);
$sqb = $b == 1 ? 1 : 2;

$mdisp = 2 * int($a / $sqb) == $a / $sqb ? $a / $sqb : '\frac{$a}{$sqb}';

$x0 = 0;
$y0 = 0;
$m  = Compute("$a/$sqb");

$mdisp = $m == 1 ? '' : $m;

$f = Formula(" $a*x/sqrt($b-x^2) ")->reduce;
$g = Formula(" $b-x^2 ");

Context("Fraction")->flags->set(reduceConstants => 1);
Context()->variables->add(u => 'Real');

$h     = Formula(" u**(-1/2)");
$num   = Formula("$a*x")->reduce;
$ntx   = Formula("-2*x");
$nhalf = Formula("-(1/2)");
$first = Formula(" $a/sqrt($b-x^2)")->reduce;
$Df1   = Formula("  ($b-x^2)^((-3)/(2))")->reduce;
$Df    = Formula(" $a/sqrt($b-x^2)+ $a*x^2/($b-x^2)^(3/2)");

Context("Numeric");
$line = Formula("$y0+$m*(x-$x0)")->reduce;

BEGIN_PGML

Find the equation of the tangent line to the graph of  [`` y(x) =[$f] ``] at [`` x = [$x0] ``].

Equation of the tangent line is [` y = `] [_]{$line}{50}
 
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

Using the product rule and [`  \small{u(x) = [$g]} `] in the generalized derivative formula for [` [$h] `] yields

 [``` 
 \begin{aligned}
 y'(x) & = \frac{d}{dx}\left[ [$f] \right] \\
 & =[$first]+\left([$num]\right)\left([$nhalf]\right)[$Df1]\left([$ntx]\right) \\
 & =  [$Df].
 \end{aligned}
 ```]

Now, when [` x = [$x0] `], [` y =  [$y0] `] and [` y'([$x0]) =  [$m] `]

Hence, equation of tangent line is [` y = [$mdisp] x `]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
